# The difference of two numbers of one limb, rounded to nearest: the step of the map sub_1
# (milestone2.md, "sum, dot, axpy, convolution": add_k, sub_k ... "the scalar operation"), as
# add_1_1 is the step of add_1. Its claims are those of add_1_1, for a - b.
kernel:        sub_1_1
input:         a
input:         b
output:        s
value:         a-b
ensures:       rounded s nearest
ensures:       error s R c=1/(1+u) k=1 t=0
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/MapSteps.v sub_1_1_correct
source:        one rounding to nearest
license:       bound: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved

s = sub(a, b)
